-- title:
--   Localised Hecke algebra into a corner ring of H¹
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation ring (a domain, complete for its maximal-ideal adic topology) with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $N, L \ge 1$ with $L \mid N$, let $S \subseteq \mathbb N$ contain every prime dividing $N$, and assume the weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ are spanned over $\mathbb C$ by [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3). Let $\theta$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}$ of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ generated by the Hecke generators away from $S$, to $k$. On $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(L), \mathcal O)$ (additive homomorphisms from [`CohCarrier.GammaH L ⊤`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133)) consider the operators [`CohCarrier.opFamily L ⊤ S 𝒪`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) attached to the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell \notin S$ prime, $\ell \nmid L$), $U_q$ ($q \mid L$ prime) and $\langle d \rangle$, assumed pairwise commuting, and let $B$ be the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O}(H^1)$ they generate. Given a residual system $\bar\theta$ of values in $k$ on the generators, let $Sp$ consist of an integer $n$, complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i \in B$ and maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ of $B$ ($i \in \mathrm{Fin}\,n$) exhausting the maximal ideals of $B$ with $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j \iff i \ne j$; fix $i_0$ and an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\pi_k$ from the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$ to $k$ sending $e_{i_0}(\mathrm{op}\,g)e_{i_0}$ to $\bar\theta(g)$ for every generator $g$. Assume $\bar\theta(T_\ell) = \theta(T_\ell)$ for all primes $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$ and $\ell \nmid N$, and that every element of the corner submodule $e_{i_0} \cdot H^1$ is a parabolic homomorphism. Then there is an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism $\varphi$ from [`CuspForm.heckeLocal N S 𝒪 θ`](def/CuspForm_HeckeLocal.html#L131), the localisation of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) attached to $\theta$ with structure map $\pi$, to the corner ring $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$ such that $\varphi(\pi(T_\ell)) = e_{i_0} T_\ell e_{i_0}$ for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$ and $\ell \nmid N$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura passage from the anemic Hecke algebra of weight-two cusp forms of level $N$, localised at a residual eigensystem $\theta$, to the Hecke algebra acting on the parabolic cohomology $H^1(\Gamma_0(L),\mathcal O)$ of a divisor level $L \mid N$, read off on a single local component cut out by an idempotent. It is what gives the modules $H^1$ on a local component their structure over the localised Hecke algebra, and it is used in the construction of the corner realisations and of the successive rungs in the modularity-lifting argument.
-- source:
